## Conclusion

So we can see that the path of the ipmitool command on Romulus is:

```
ipmitool -> D-Bus -> phosphor-ipmi-host
```

There's no any system interface involved in the path, and it is interpreted as `INTRABMC` in phosphor-ipmi-host.

Therefore, the command
```
ipmitool raw 0x04 0x02 0x21 0x04 0x01 0x01 0x01 0x59 0x01 0x00
```
on Romulus is not exercising the System Interface parsing path.

The previous implementation accepted this payload only because
`isFromSystemChannel()` always returned `true`, so every request was
parsed as System Interface format.

With this patch, payload decoding is selected based on the actual
incoming channel rather than always assuming the System Interface
format. Therefore, an 8-byte System Interface payload is rejected when
received through INTRABMC.

I hope this finding solve your question ^^.
Please let me know if you think I have misunderstood the request path or if there is another scenario that you would like me to verify.
